# Desktop overlay UX

## Shape and surface
- One cream `#shell` that morphs — do not add a separate left cream card beside the session rail.
- Boxy rounded corners (`~14px`), not pill/`border-radius: 999px` on the shell.
- Session-time rail stays on the docked edge (right/left/top): green fill grows with study progress; no grey XP track or level badge.

## Open / close motion
- Prefer one native `setBounds(bounds, true)` morph (closed ↔ open) over stepped frame loops or no-op mid stages.
- Open (sides): widen at closed strip height (content square + `barThickness` for the session rail), then fade content in.
- Open (top): grow thickness to content square + rail, then fade content in.
- Close: fade content out, then reverse the same morph back to the strip.
- Respect reduced motion (instant bounds, no waits). Keep `panelToggleSeq` so rapid toggles cancel stale timeouts.

## Pet
- Closed bar: anchor the pet beside the session rail (`barThickness`).
- Open bar: hide the external pet window and show the pet inside the cream shell; restore the external pet when closing a distracted tab (walk animation).
- Drag from the pet only (closed external sprite or open in-panel sprite); show `grab` / `grabbing` cursor on the pet; the session rail opens/closes the bar; no drag handle; no bottom dock target (left/right/top only).
- Session rail shows a centered chevron that points toward expand when closed and the opposite when open (per dock edge).
- Chat bubbles sit above the pet with a sharp triangle tip (fade in). No-session copy prompts starting on the web; live distraction / close copy show for open or closed; open-bar-only idle lines stay in-panel.

## Do not
- Invent XP or change session/score APIs for overlay polish.
- Leave a large transparent window after close that blocks other apps.
